      "content": "The core weakness of Democratic Socialism is its inherent contradiction between the demand for massive state control and the promotion of individual liberty. By advocating for extensive wealth redistribution and government management of key industries, they fundamentally undermine the free-market principles that drive innovation and personal economic freedom. Furthermore, their reliance on ever-increasing taxation to fund these expansive programs creates an unsustainable fiscal model that inevitably stifles economic growth.",
